{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat assignments/T-QRT-qwen-routing-skew.md'","aggregated_output":"# Assignment T-QRT (campaign c2-resume, x86-main; owner Claude Opus; worker Codex) — should we build expert-granular placement for Qwen3-30B-A3B? Measure routing skew first.\nContext: decisions/D030/D031 (hybrid hot/cold expert split lost on Granite because per-layer handoff dominates small 0.84 MiB experts), D039 (Qwen3-30B-A3B: 48 layers x 128 experts top-8, 2.72 MiB/expert; CPU expert path ~30 GB/s; 0.757 ms per CPU layer; layer offload frontier measured). The decision depends on routing skew: what fraction of routed (token, expert) requests a per-layer hot set of H experts covers.\nDo: (1) Read cc/routing_trace/README.md + tools: determine whether its trace patch/tool is architecture-generic or Granite-only; if Granite-only, make the minimal extension for qwen3moe (patch in cc/routing_trace/, against 31288c9c6). (2) Build CPU-only in a scratch tree (artifacts/codexQRT/tree, -DGGML_CUDA=OFF, -j4, nice) and record routing for Qwen3-30B-A3B (~/models/campaign/qwen3-30b-a3b/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Q4_K_M.gguf, mmap, -t 8) on TRAIN prompt artifacts/traces/in/prose.txt (prefill) and EVAL prompts artifacts/traces/in/chat.txt (+ code.txt if present), generating ~64 tokens each (CPU decode ~5-10 t/s is fine). (3) Run `python3 cc/model_inspect/inspect_model.py <gguf> --trace <trace>` (adapt the trace adapter if needed) to get per-layer coverage curves; compute held-out coverage (hot set ranked on TRAIN, evaluated on EVAL) for hot-set sizes matching GPU byte budgets of static K in {8,18,30,42}. (4) Predict decode t/s for an expert-granular split at those budgets with the D039 model: 1/decode = t_gpu + 48 layers x [(1-coverage) x 8 x 2.72 MiB / 30 GB/s] + n_cpu_layers x t_handoff (t_handoff: estimate from D031, state range), and compare to the measured static frontier (D039). State the predicted crossover and whether building a qwen3moe CUDA hybrid (with batched skip-ID dispatch per T-PROF) is justified.\nAllowed writes: cc/routing_trace/** (only additive arch support), artifacts/codexQRT/**. 75 min, no Docker/GPU, -j4, nice; never fill RAM: Qwen mmap ~18.6 GB of 46 GB host RAM — run ONE process at a time. Final message: generic-or-not, trace sizes/sha, coverage table (train vs eval), predicted vs static frontier, recommendation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
