med only when owned containers are gone)\n  lab status [JOB]                  states\n  lab reconcile                     inspect non-terminal attempts against REAL processes/containers; never trusts heartbeats\n  lab register JOB ATT              register result into index (idempotent; stale/conflicting rejected)\nStore: $LAB/{images,jobs,index}. Fault injection for recovery tests: LAB_FAULT=die_after_start|die_in_export\n\"\"\"\nimport json, sys, os, re, time, uuid, Explain, step by step, how a mixture-of-experts transformer routes each token to a small subset of experts, why that saves compute, and what problems appear when the expert weights do not fit in GPU memory. Then propose three practical strategies and compare their trade-offs in a short table.\nanka and renga . He was the first to write a commentary on Du Fu 's poetry in Japan . \n In the Edo period , the influence of Du Fu became more pronounced . The poet Matsuo Bashō , who was deeply influenced by Du Fu 's poetry , wrote a famous haiku about the poet\n a.att, \"evidence.json\"), dict(chaos=now(), containers=cs))\n\ndef owned_containers(att, token):\n    # returns list of containers owned by this attempt (based on token)\n    # (this is a simplified model; in reality, containers are tagged with the job/att and token\n    1 artifacts/traces/in/chat.txt\n   96 artifacts/traces/in/code.txt\n   17 artifacts/traces/in/prose.txt\n  114 total\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
