{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('artifacts/codexQRT/write_report.py'); s=p.read_text()\nstart=s.index(\\\"lines+=['',\\\\n'The coverage crossover\\\")\nend=s.index(\\\"lines+=['', '## Recommendation'\\\",start)\ns=s[:start]+'''lines+=['',\n'The coverage crossover sets the requested latency equation equal to each measured static point. The maximum handoff is the residual latency margin divided by 48; dispatch overhead beyond t_gpu must fit inside that same margin. K=8 and K=18 already lose at zero handoff. K=30 crosses parity at 44.44% coverage for a 50 us handoff; measured held-out coverage is only 44.96%. Its entire remaining margin is about 0.193 ms/token. K=42 requires 20.39% coverage at 50 us but achieves 15.26%; it would need handoff below 11.02 us, outside the estimated range. Thus there is no robust crossover across the requested budgets.', '',\n'Each domain is itself skewed: mean per-layer prefill entropy is 5.471 bits for prose, 5.488 for chat, and 5.410 for code, versus a 7-bit uniform maximum; separately fitted descriptive hot sets reach 90% coverage at mean H=42.92, 41.02, and 43.10 respectively. This does not mean prose-selected experts transfer to code. Low cross-domain coverage is evidence against this particular TRAIN policy, not proof that all expert placement policies fail.']\n''' +s[end:]\ns=s.replace('RECOMMENDATION_PLACEHOLDER', 'Do not prioritize a general qwen3moe CUDA hybrid on this TRAIN/EVAL evidence. At 30-80 us handoff, the pooled forecasts lose at K=8,18,42; K=30 spans 35.0-38.2 t/s versus static 36.6, with only a 0.7% central gain. The required batched skip-ID dispatch is a prerequisite, but its unknown incremental cost can erase that small gain. First validate hot sets trained on a larger, diverse and deployment-matched corpus against longer held-out continuations. A domain-specific prototype could be reconsidered if held-out coverage clears the listed thresholds with enough margin to pay dispatch, allocation and handoff costs. Preserve original selected-slot order/numerics, batch CUDA skip-ID expert dispatch, and measure actual Qwen handoffs before claiming speedup. This assignment measures routing and forecasts; it does not validate a hybrid implementation.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 artifacts/codexQRT/write_report.py\nsed -n '1,155p' artifacts/codexQRT/ANALYSIS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
